<resources>
    <style name="Theme.NewsRSSReader" parent="android:Theme.Material.Light.NoActionBar" />

    <!--
      Launch-time theme installed via the AndroidX Splash Screen API (see MainActivity's
      installSplashScreen() call). It owns the window only until the first frame is drawn, at
      which point the library swaps the activity's theme back to Theme.NewsRSSReader. Using it
      keeps the cold-start splash consistent across Android versions instead of relying on the
      OS auto-deriving one from the adaptive launcher icon (inconsistent pre-12, and varies by
      launcher).

      The icon drawable used here (@drawable/ic_lenta_logo_splash) is the white "LENTA"
      wordmark centered on a padded, transparent square canvas (see that drawable's own comment)
      so the Splash Screen API's forced square-plus-circle-mask icon slot doesn't stretch or crop
      it - it renders small but fully intact and proportional, blending onto the solid black
      windowSplashScreenBackground below.
    -->
    <style name="Theme.NewsRSSReader.Splash" parent="Theme.SplashScreen">
        <item name="windowSplashScreenBackground">#000000</item>
        <item name="windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon">@drawable/ic_lenta_logo_splash</item>
        <item name="postSplashScreenTheme">@style/Theme.NewsRSSReader</item>
    </style>
</resources>
